+# FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix 7b49ecf357 (crbug 585625640), the M156 merge of V8 15.6.75.81
+
+SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 24-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0003`). M156 merge 7b49ecf357 (bugs
+587681267 and 585625640) on branch-heads/15.6, applied as is to 15.6.75.66. Severity not published.
+
+- `CommonOperatorReducer::ReducePhi` could turn a `0 < v ? v : 0 - v` Phi into a `Word32Select`. If an input was a
+  `TypeGuard`, which has no control output, the scheduler had to hoist it past the Merge, so a type valid on only one side
+  of the branch was applied on both. That is a type confusion in optimized code. The reducer now skips the reduction when
+  the inputs are `TypeGuard`s (`node-properties.h` gains the helper).
+- `common-operator-reducer.cc` and `node-properties.h` are not touched by any other `patches/v8` file. Test
+  `regress/wasm/regress-585625640.js`.
+
+**Cache epoch:** covered by the single 40 -> 41 bump of `siguiente-3` (`brave-core/0001`).
+
+To check (D8-LINUX): mjsunit `regress/wasm/regress-585625640` and `compiler/*`.
+
 # FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix c20e1a6e22 (crbug 581560002), ported from the M159 merge
 
 SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 24-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0002`). **Not merged to V8 15.6
